    "MagneticTB", "status" -> "None", "summary" -> 
    "MagneticTB 2.0 includes the functions from version 1.0. To continue \
using a 1.0 notebook, load MagneticTBOld` and use the function names ending \
in old. The graphene example below shows how to initialize a model, calculate \
its Hamiltonian, and plot the bands with these functions. Start a fresh \
kernel and load MagneticTBOld` with the following command. Use separate \
kernels for versions 1.0 and 2.0: For graphene, give the hexagonal lattice, \
one representative carbon position, and its pz orbital. The symmetry \
operations generate the second carbon atom. In version 1.0, the function and \
option names below all end in old:", "synonyms" -> {}, "tabletags" -> {}, 
    "title" -> "Using MagneticTB 1.0", "titlemodifier" -> "", 
